--  Translation of types

--  A single type declaration in Ada can give rise to several Why3 modules.
--  Translate_Type introduces its representation and operation symbols;
--  Generate_Type_Completion supplies definitions that may reference entities
--  declared after the type. Generate_VCs_For_Type creates independent checks
--  for the type declaration. Checks depending on the values of local
--  variables are generated at the point of declaration by Gnat2Why.Expr.

--  Scalar representations include mathematical integers, bitvectors, IEEE
--  floating-point values, and scaled integers for fixed point. Conversion
--  functions connect scalars modeled by distinct Why3 types to their
--  representative types; see Why.Gen.Scalars. Arrays use maps and bounds, with
--  shared representative modules; see Why.Gen.Arrays.

--  Records are a bit special because there cannot be a "universal" record
--  type in Why, as e.g. for integer types. Instead, we use Why records which
--  directly correspond to the Ada definition. All operations (i.e. field
--  accesses) are defined on the type itself. To deal with conversions between
--  records, we use the same idea as for the other Ada types. However, the
--  underlying model type now is the root type for each record type. The root
--  type is the one that has been introduced with an explicit "record ... end
--  record" scheme, as opposed to a derived type or subtype.

--  Note that the frontend differentiates between a private type and its
--  completion (two different entities), while gnat2why does not look at
--  private types and goes to the actual type (either the completion, or
--  further up if the completion is a derived type of a private type ...)

--  There is an exception to that rule, namely for private types whose
--  completion is not in SPARK. Such types *are* in SPARK, and in this
--  case gnat2why *only* looks at the private entity.

--  The main type completion module (module kind Axiom) defines dynamic
--  invariants, non-static scalar bounds, and initialization predicates.
--  Default initialization, type invariants, user equality and dispatching
--  equality definitions, and move trees have separate modules.
--  Tagged types also need representative completions and tag compatibility
--  axioms. Subtype predicates are inlined in dynamic invariants rather than
--  declared as separate predicate symbols. Why.Atree.Modules identifies
--  module kinds; Why.Inter records dependencies and selects function axioms
--  for proofs.

--  Access-to-object types designating incomplete types, and their
--  initialization wrappers, have representative completions connecting
--  abstract designated values to their completed type.
--  These are generated by Translate_Type when the designated full view is
--  translated. Their encoding is described in Why.Gen.Pointers; see also
--  Gnat2Why.Subprograms.Pointers for access-to-subprogram call models.

with SPARK_Atree.Entities; use SPARK_Atree.Entities;
with Why.Ids;              use Why.Ids;

package Gnat2Why.Types is

   procedure Translate_Type (E : Type_Kind_Id);
   --  Generate the Why3 declaration module for the type entity in argument.
   --  Dispatch to the representation packages for scalars, records, arrays,
   --  and access types, and declare any additional type modules needed.

   function Ident_Of_Ada_Type (E : Type_Kind_Id) return W_Name_Id;
   --  Transform the type entity in argument to an identifier. This function
   --  works with Boolean, but not with things like Universal_Integer.

   procedure Generate_Type_Completion (E : Type_Kind_Id);
   --  Generate the completion modules for type E
   --
   --  The main completion defines dynamic invariants, non-static scalar
   --  bounds, and initialization predicates for composite wrappers. It also
   --  completes tagged representations and access-to-subprogram call models.
   --  Named dynamic invariants and default initial assumptions are not created
   --  for Itypes: their properties are computed at each use, where local
   --  inputs such as 'Old values are available.

   procedure Generate_VCs_For_Type (E : Type_Kind_Id);
   --  Generate a module for the VCs associated to a type declaration. We
   --  isolate in this separate module those checks that should be done
   --  independently from the value of variables at the point of declaration.

end Gnat2Why.Types;
